at your option.

WHY BOTH. This is the Rust ecosystem's convention and it exists because the two licenses cover
different worries. MIT is short and universally understood. Apache-2.0 adds an explicit patent
grant and a patent-retaliation clause, which some organizations require before they will take a
dependency. Offering both means neither preference blocks adoption.

CONTRIBUTIONS. Unless you state otherwise, any contribution you intentionally submit for inclusion
in this work — as defined in the Apache-2.0 license — shall be dual-licensed as above, with no
additional terms or conditions. Inbound equals outbound; there is no CLA.

THIRD-PARTY CODE. This repository builds against Elixir and Erlang/OTP and a small set of Hex
packages, each under its own license. See THIRD_PARTY.md for the full inventory.
